sophageal cancer resection outcomes.INT J EPIDEMIOL:International Journal of Epidemiology publishes studies related to epidemiology, including cancer research and body mass index analysis.AMERICAN COLLEGE OF SURGEONS:The American College of Surgeons is a professional organization that evaluates patient care and outcomes in surgical practices, including esophageal cancer.CANCER CACHEXIA:Cancer cachexia is a complex syndrome that significantly impacts cancer patients, characterized by severe body weight loss, muscle mass depletion, and alterations in metabolism. This condition often involves not only the loss of muscle but also fat, leading to a notable decline in overall body composition. It is frequently observed in patients with advanced stages of cancer, particularly those suffering from pancreatic and esophageal cancers. The syndrome is associated with decreased appetite, which further exacerbates the nutritional challenges faced by these patients. Due to its profound effects on health and quality of life, cancer cachexia has become a significant focus of research within the field of oncology, highlighting the need for specialized nutritional interventions and support to manage this debilitating condition effectively.SERUM C-REACTIVE PROTEIN:Serum C-reactive protein is a marker that is studied in relation to prognosis in esophageal carcinoma.GLASGOW PROGNOSTIC SCORE:The Glasgow Prognostic Score is a clinical tool used to predict outcomes in cancer patients, particularly those with esophageal cancer.PREOPERATIVE WEIGHT LOSS:Preoperative weight loss is a condition studied in relation to postoperative outcomes in esophageal cancer patients.POSTOPERATIVE COURSE:Postoperative course refers to the recovery process following surgery, particularly in esophageal cancer resection.NEOADJUVANT CHEMOTHERAPY:Neoadjuvant chemotherapy is a treatment given before surgery to shrink tumors, often used in patients with esophageal cancer to improve surgical outcomes.CRITICAL REVIEWS IN ONCOLOGY HEMATOLOGY:Critical Reviews in Oncology Hematology is a journal that publishes reviews on various aspects of oncology and hematology, including cancer cachexia and its management.EUROPEAN RADIOL:European Radiology is a journal that publishes research on radiology, including studies related to cancer treatment and outcomes.RESTING ENERGY EXPENDITURE:Resting energy expenditure refers to the amount of energy expended while at rest, which can be affected in patients with esophageal cancer and cachexia.CIRCULATING LEPTIN:Circulating leptin is a hormone involved in regulating energy balance and can be altered in patients with esophageal cancer and cachexia.CLINICAL DETERMINANTS:Clinical determinants refer to factors that influence weight loss in patients with esophageal carcinoma during treatment, including radiotherapy.CHEMORADIOTHERAPY:Chemoradiotherapy is a combined treatment approach using chemotherapy and radiation therapy, often employed in the management of esophageal cancer.GHRL:Ghrelin is a hormone that plays a role in regulating appetite and is mentioned in relation to body weight loss after esophagectomy for esophageal cancer.MARTIN:Martin is a researcher focused on the studies of weight loss and nutritional status in patients with esophageal cancer. He has also investigated the risk factors associated with weight loss in survivors of esophageal cancer. Through his work, Martin contributes valuable insights into the challenges faced by this patient population, aiming to improve their health outcomes and quality of life.WEIJS:Weijs is a researcher who contributed to the study on nutritional support for patients with esophageal cancer.TE BOVELDT:Te Boveldt is a researcher mentioned in the context of studies related to esophageal cancer and nutritional interventions.BUSKERMOLEN:Buskermolen is a researcher involved in the studies regarding nutritional support for esophageal cancer patients.EARTHMAN:Earthman is a researcher who has contributed to the studies on nutritional support in esophageal cancer patients.VERHEUL:Verheul is a researcher mentioned in the context of studies on postoperative complications in esophageal cancer.WANG:Wang is a researcher who conducted a comparison study on early enteral nutrition in esophageal cancer patients.CHEN:Chen is a researcher involved in studies comparing nutritional approaches for esophageal cancer patients.LIU:Liu is a researcher who contributed to the studies on postoperative nutrition in esophageal cancer patients.MA:Ma is a researcher mentioned in the context of studies on nutritional support for esophageal cancer patients.JIA:Jia is a researcher involved in studies comparing nutritional strategies for esophageal cancer patients.PENG:Peng is a researcher who conducted a meta-analysis on enteral versus parenteral nutrition for esophageal cancer patients.CAI:Cai is a researcher involved in the meta-analysis comparing nutritional approaches for esophageal cancer patients.NIU:Niu is a researcher mentioned in the context of studies on nutritional support for esophageal cancer patients.LAGERGREN:Lagergren is a researcher involved in studies on long-term weight change after esophageal cancer surgery.D'JOURNO:D'Journo is a researcher who studied the prognostic impact of weight loss in esophageal cancer survivors.KOIZUMI:Koizumi is a researcher who studied the relationship between ghrelin levels and weight loss after esophagectomy.MIYAZAKI:Miyazaki is a researcher involved in studies on ghrelin levels and body weight loss in esophageal cancer patients.DOKI:Doki is a researcher who studied the correlation between ghrelin reduction and postoperative weight loss in esophageal cancer patients.KARAGIANNI:Karagianni is a researcher who studied nutritional status and support before and after pancreatectomy for pancreatic cancer.KIM:Kim is a researcher mentioned in the context of studies related to nutritional support in cancer patients.LIGTHART-MELIS:MASSACHUSETTS GENERAL HOSPITAL:Massachusetts General Hospital is a teaching hospital in Boston, known for its surgical procedures, including the Whipple procedure for pancreatic cancer.WHIPPLE PROCEDURE:The Whipple procedure is a complex surgery performed to remove the head of the pancreas, often used in the treatment of pancreatic cancer.PAPALOIS AE:Papalois AE is an author involved in the study of nutritional support before and after pancreatectomy for pancreatic cancer.TRIANTAFILLIDIS JK:Triantafillidis JK is an author who co-authored research on nutritional status in pancreatic cancer patients.KIM SY:Kim SY is an author who studied changes in dietary intake and nutritional status in pancreatic cancer patients.RICHARD E:Richter E is an author who researched parental nutrition support for patients with pancreatic cancer.GOONETILLEKE KS:Goonetilleke KS is an author who conducted a systematic review of nutritional supplementation in pancreaticoduodenectomy patients.PORTA M:Porta M is an author who researched symptoms at presentation in exocrine pancreatic cancer patients.BYE A:Bye A is an author who studied the importance of symptoms in advanced pancreatic cancer for energy intake.LA TORRE M:La Torre M is an author who researched malnutrition and outcomes in pancreatic surgery.BOSSOLA M:Bossola M is an author advocating for more clinical trials on cancer cachexia.FERRONE CR:Ferrone CR is an author involved in the evolution of the Whipple procedure at Massachusetts General Hospital.KANDA M:Kanda M is an author who studied nutritional predictors of postoperative outcomes in pancreatic cancer.KARAGIANNI VT:JPEN J PARENTER ENTERAL NUTR:JPEN J PARENTER ENTERAL NUTR, also known as the Journal of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (JPEN), is a scholarly journal dedicated to the publication of research and guidelines concerning parenteral and enteral nutrition. It serves as a vital platform for advancements in nutritional practices, focusing on both clinical and research aspects of nutrition therapy. The journal encompasses a wide range of topics, including studies on immunonutrition and its effects on surgical outcomes, thereby contributing to the understanding and improvement of nutritional interventions in various medical contexts. Through its comprehensive coverage of research related to nutrition therapy, JPEN plays a significant role in enhancing the field of parenteral and enteral nutrition.SURGICAL ONCOLOGY:A journal focused on the field of surgical oncology, publishing studies on cancer treatment and outcomes, including immunonutrition.NUTRITION AND CANCER:A journal that explores the relationship between nutrition and cancer, including studies on immunonutrition and its effects on cancer patients.EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF SURGICAL ONCOLOGY:A journal that publishes research on surgical oncology, including studies on the efficacy of immunonutrition in cancer surgeries.ARCHIVES OF IMMUNOLOGY AND THERAPY EXPERIMENTAL:A journal that publishes research on immunology and its applications in therapy, including studies on immunonutrition in cancer patients.CLINICAL SCIENCE:A journal that publishes research on clinical and experimental medicine, including studies on the effects of immunonutrition in cancer patients.ZHANG Y:Zhang Y is a researcher with a focus on the study of inflammatory cytokines and food allergies. Additionally, Zhang Y is involved in the systematic review of perioperative immunonutrition specifically for gastrointestinal cancer. This dual focus highlights Zhang Y's commitment to advancing knowledge in both immunological responses related to food allergies and nutritional strategies in the context of cancer treatment.GU Y:Gu Y is a researcher who co-authored studies on the effects of immunonutrition in surgical patients.GUO T:Guo T is a researcher who has contributed to the systematic review of immunonutrition in gastrointestinal cancer.LI Y:Li Y is a researcher involved in studies on perioperative immunonutrition for gastrointestinal cancer.CAI H:Cai H is a researcher who co-authored studies on immunonutrition in surgical oncology.GADE J:Gade J is a researcher who has studied the effects of preoperative oral immunonutrition on surgical outcomes.LEVRING T:Levring T is a researcher involved in studies on immunonutrition and its impact on surgical recovery.HILLINGS√ò J:Hillings√∏ J is a researcher who has contributed to studies on immunonutrition in surgical patients.HANSEN CP:Hansen CP is a researcher involved in studies on the effects of immunonutrition in surgery.ANDERSEN JR:Andersen JR is a researcher who has studied the effects of preoperative immunonutrition.MARTIN RC 2ND:Martin RC 2nd is a researcher who has published studies on the efficacy of preoperative immunonutrition in pancreatic cancer.AGLE S:Agle S is a researcher involved in studies on immunonutrition and surgical outcomes.SCHLEGEL M:Schlegel M is a researcher who has contributed to studies on immunonutrition in surgical oncology.HAYAT T:Hayat T is a researcher involved in studies on immunonutrition and its effects on surgical patients.SCOGGINS CR:Scoggins CR is a researcher who has studied the role of immunonutrition in surgical recovery.MCMASTERS KM:McMasters KM is a researcher involved in studies on immunonutrition in pancreatic cancer surgery.S≈ÅOTWI≈ÉSKI R:S≈Çotwi≈Ñski R is a researcher who has studied the effects of immunonutrition on lymphocytes in pancreatic cancer patients.OLSZEWSKI W:Olszewski W is a researcher involved in studies on systemic immune dysfunction in pancreatic cancer patients.S≈ÅODKOWSKI M:S≈Çodkowski M is a researcher who has contributed to studies on immunonutrition in surgical oncology.LECH G:Lech G is a researcher involved in studies on immunonutrition and its effects on surgical outcomes.ZALESKA M:Zaleska M is a researcher who has studied the impact of immunonutrition on surgical recovery.KƒòDZIORA S:Kƒôdziora S is a researcher involved in studies on immunonutrition in cancer patients.SHIRAKAWA H:Shirakawa H is a researcher 