re used to treat certain cancers and blood disorders by replacing damaged bone marrow with healthy stem cells."}{"title": "GLUTAMINE SUPPLEMENTATION:Glutamine supplementation is a nutritional intervention that involves the use of glutamine, an amino acid, to enhance health outcomes in various populations. It is particularly aimed at preventing morbidity and mortality in preterm infants, highlighting its importance in neonatal care. Additionally, glutamine supplementation is utilized to improve health outcomes in critically ill patients and those undergoing specific medical treatments, demonstrating its broader application in clinical settings."}{"title": "HSIAO VC:Hsiao VC is an author involved in the study of hyperglycemia and its association with neutropenic infections."}{"title": "SAUDEK CD:Saudek CD is an author who researched the effects of hyperglycemia during bone marrow transplantation."}{"title": "OUDMANS-VAN STRAATEN HM:Oudemans-van Straaten HM is an author who studied plasma glutamine depletion in acute ICU admissions."}{"title": "BOSMAN RJ:Bosman RJ is an author who contributed to research on patient outcomes in acute ICU admissions."}{"title": "TRESKES M:Treskes M is an author involved in the study of plasma glutamine and its effects on patient outcomes."}{"title": "DECHELOTTE P:D\u00e9chelotte P is an author who researched the effects of glutamine supplementation in critically ill patients."}{"title": "HASSELMANN M:Hasselmann M is an author who contributed to the study of glutamine in total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "SOUBA WW:Souba WW is an author who studied intestinal glutamine metabolism and its implications for nutrition."}{"title": "ALPERS D:Alpers D is an author who discussed the evidence for glutamine supplementation in humans."}{"title": "HERRERA-MART\u00cdNEZ AD:Herrera-Mart\u00ednez AD is an author who studied the use of glutamine in total parenteral nutrition for bone marrow transplant patients."}{"title": "ANDERSON P:Anderson P is an